  "answer": "Fats are digested in the small intestine. The process begins when bile juice from the liver is released into the small intestine. This bile juice helps convert fats into small globule-like forms, a process called emulsification. This makes the fats easier for enzymes to act on. The pancreatic juice from the pancreas contains an enzyme called lipase, which further breaks down the fats into fatty acids and glycerol. These are the end products of fat digestion.",
